{"name":"Nursery","hex":"#efd0d2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nursery","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place where nursing (“breastfeeding”) or the raising of children is carried on.\n Especially in European countries: a room or area in a household set apart for the care of children.\n\n An institution for small children who not yet have begun primary school during daytime (when their parents work); a daycare centre.","Especially in European countries: a room or area in a household set apart for the care of children."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nursery"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nursery (room)","blocks":[{"text":"A nursery is a bedroom within a house or other dwelling set aside for an infant or toddler."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Baby_nursery_room.jpg/330px-Baby_nursery_room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nursery_(room)","wikidata":"Q1741939"},{"title":"Preschool","blocks":[{"text":"A preschool, also known as pre-primary school, play school, or nursery school, is an educational establishment or learning space offering early childhood education to children before they begin compulsory education at primary school. It may be publicly or privately operated and may be subsidized from public funds. The typical age range for preschool in most countries is from 2 to 6 years."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Tawau_Sabah_Tadika-Holy-Trinity-22.jpg/330px-Tawau_Sabah_Tadika-Holy-Trinity-22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Preschool","wikidata":"Q1076052"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Barnkammare_-_Nordiska_museet_-_NMA.0097400.jpg/500px-Barnkammare_-_Nordiska_museet_-_NMA.0097400.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c